hub.com/users/filters-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/filters-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-28T00:41:11Z","updated_at":"2026-11-28T00:41:11Z","body":"<!-- adguard-filters-agent:report {\"schemaVersion\":1,\"revisionDigest\":\"95b3f9f3a4b7613a8a3f899545b46df81748570e26f4aaec700ffd26fb4dc6cf\"} -->\nAnalysis-only findings, no verified change\n\n## Reproduced symptom\n\nIndeterminate — polybuzz.ai serves the reporter's overlay ads from a page-owned full-document ad container, div#⁠character-chat-ad-layer, fed by the Venatus (hb.vntsm.com) and MGID loaders; with the reporter's own filters those loaders are already blocked on network-level platforms, so the overlay did not render in any live capture or rehearsal and apply_rule could not judge the element-hiding rule (inconclusive, baseline_symptom_absent). Candidate for maintainer review:⁠ polybuzz.ai#⁠#⁠.character-chat-ad-layer in BaseFilter/sections/specific.txt right after the existing polybuzz.ai#⁠#⁠.infeed-ad rule (line 4494) — the likely iOS gap is that Base's Venatus rule relies on $redirect, which Safari content blockers do not support.\n\n## Candidate for review\n\n`polybuzz.ai##.character-chat-ad-layer`\n\nBaseFilter/sections/specific.txt\n\nNot verified: apply_rule came back environmentExperiment:⁠ inconclusive with errorKind baseline_symptom_absent and validationSkipped:⁠ true — under the reporter's own four filters (Base, Mobile Ads, Tracking Protection, Mail Tracking Protection) the Venatus (hb.vntsm.com, $redirect=noopjs) and MGID loaders are already stopped, so div#⁠character-chat-ad-layer stays empty and no overlay ad renders to compare in any phase; the candidate was never judged, i.e. an environment limit, not a rejected rule. The reporter (AdGuard for iOS) still sees the ads; per the compatibility guidance $redirect is unsupported by SafariConverterLib, so the rule that stops the Venatus SDK/loader on network-level platforms cannot act in the iOS app and its ads can be painted into that page-owned layer, where a content-blocker-supported element-hiding rule would still hide them. Unverified:⁠ no iOS execution model available, so neither the iOS gap nor the effect of hiding the layer could be observed.\n\n## Artifacts\n\nhttps://github.com/AdguardTeam/AdguardFilters/actions/runs/46088446696\n\n<sub>Automated analysis against filters at `c2a42bb`. Posted by a filters agent; a maintainer reviews before anything is merged.</sub>\n","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AdguardTeam/AdguardFilters/issues/comments/7231112765/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}},"public":true,"created_at":"2026-11-28T00:41:11Z","org":{"id":8361145,"login":"AdguardTeam","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/orgs/AdguardTeam","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8361145?"}}
